{"id":147,"date":"2022-04-22T04:59:53","date_gmt":"2022-04-22T04:59:53","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/fisat.ac.in\/?page_id=147"},"modified":"2026-07-11T14:41:36","modified_gmt":"2026-07-11T14:41:36","slug":"institution","status":"publish","type":"page","link":"https:\/\/fisat.ac.in\/institution\/","title":{"rendered":"The Institution"},"content":{"rendered":"\r\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>The Federal Institute of Science and Technology (FISAT)<\/strong> is a self-financing private engineering college established and promoted by the <strong>Federal Bank Officers\u2019 Association Educational Society (FBOAES)<\/strong>. FBOAES is an initiative of the <strong>Federal Bank Officers\u2019 Association (FBOA)<\/strong>, the sole representative body of all Federal Bank officers.<\/p>\r\n<p>FISAT occupies a unique position in South India\u2019s professional education sector. Established in 2002 with the motto <strong>\u201cFocus on Excellence,\u201d<\/strong> the institution has been designed and developed as a <strong>Centre of Excellence<\/strong> in professional education. Over the years, FISAT has carved a niche for itself through its students\u2019 outstanding achievements in academics, placements, research, innovation, and co-curricular and extra-curricular activities. The institution continues to pursue its vision of delivering quality education while nurturing competent professionals and responsible citizens.<\/p>\r\n<p>In recognition of its academic excellence and robust governance, the <strong>University Grants Commission (UGC)<\/strong> conferred <strong>Autonomous Status<\/strong> on FISAT for a period of <strong>10 years in 2025<\/strong>. The institution is accredited with an <strong>&#8216;A+&#8217; Grade<\/strong> by the <strong>National Assessment and Accreditation Council (NAAC)<\/strong> in its second accreditation cycle. Six B.Tech programmes are accredited by the <strong>National Board of Accreditation (NBA)<\/strong>. Demonstrating its commitment to quality management and continuous improvement in education, FISAT is also <strong>ISO 21001:2018 Educational Organizations Management System (EOMS) certified<\/strong>.<\/p>\r\n<p>FISAT is located at <strong>Hormis Nagar<\/strong>, Mookkannoor, near Angamaly in Ernakulam District, Kerala, the birthplace of <strong>Late K. P. Hormis<\/strong>, the founder of <strong>The Federal Bank Ltd.<\/strong>, after whom the campus is named.<\/p>\r\n<p>The institution is affiliated with <strong>APJ Abdul Kalam Technological University (KTU)<\/strong> and approved by the <strong>All India Council for Technical Education (AICTE), New Delhi<\/strong>. FISAT offers seven <strong>B.Tech<\/strong> programmes, an <strong>MBA<\/strong> programme with specialisations in Finance, Marketing, Human Resource Management, Information Systems, Production &amp; Operations Management, and International Business, an <strong>MCA<\/strong> programme, an <strong>Integrated MCA<\/strong> programme, five <strong>M.Tech<\/strong> programmes, and <strong>Ph.D.<\/strong> programmes in various disciplines.<\/p>\r\n","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"<p>The Federal Institute of Science and Technology (FISAT) is a self-financing private engineering college established and promoted by the Federal Bank Officers\u2019 Association Educational Society (FBOAES). FBOAES is an initiative of the Federal Bank Officers\u2019 Association (FBOA), the sole representative body of all Federal Bank officers. FISAT occupies a unique position in South India\u2019s professional [&hellip;]<\/p>\n","protected":false},"author":2,"featured_media":2591,"parent":0,"menu_order":0,"comment_status":"closed","ping_status":"closed","template":"","meta":{"_acf_changed":false,"footnotes":""},"class_list":["post-147","page","type-page","status-publish","has-post-thumbnail","hentry"],"acf":[],"_links":{"self":[{"href":"https:\/\/fisat.ac.in\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/pages\/147","targetHints":{"allow":["GET"]}}],"collection":[{"href